## Summary
In this video, Vince Buyssens reviews visual references to guide AI agents in designing a cohesive diagram and UI system for Thoughtform's proposals and website. He uses Pinterest to showcase 2D terminal interfaces, clean mathematical visualizations, and isometric technical drawings, contrasting them with a local animated 3D hologram artifact to outline rules for when to use 2D versus 3D elements while maintaining a unified sci-fi aesthetic.

## Segments
[00:00.0-00:48.8] Vince is on a Pinterest board titled "INTERFACES 2 U", clicking on a cyan orbital diagram and then a green terminal interface pin.
[00:48.8-01:29.8] The screen switches to a local HTML file displaying a rotating 3D holographic artifact with concentric rings and a waveform, which he pans and zooms.
[01:29.8-03:51.6] Vince returns to Pinterest, scrolling and opening various diagram pins, including a vertical flowchart, a circular neon process visualization, and several isometric plots and technical drawings.
[03:51.6-04:33.6] He switches away from Pinterest, briefly showing a Notion document next to an image, then the Atreides company website, and finally opening the Windows Start menu while finishing his thought.

