## Rules
2D diagrams must feel like part of the same design language as the 3D artifacts.
The center of the main artifact represents the Thoughtform brand mark.
The left side of the main artifact represents upstream data; the right side represents downstream data.
Use simple animations to convey flow or meaning.
3D elements should be used sparingly.
Small UI icons inside frames must be 2D, not 3D.
Designs should fit a terminal interface aesthetic or technical manual leitmotif.

## Synthesis
The desired diagram system is a cohesive blend of 2D and 3D elements inspired by retro-futuristic terminal interfaces and holographic data displays. The system uses a strict hierarchy: complex, large-scale visualizations and technical manual motifs can utilize 3D isometric or perspective wireframes, while smaller, functional UI elements and basic process flows must remain clean, 2D line art. The core visual language relies on glowing geometric primitives against dark backgrounds, anchored by a central brand identity ("thoughtform") that maps systemic flows from upstream to downstream. The overarching challenge is seamlessly integrating these 2D and 3D styles without causing visual discombobulation.

